Normality of salt solution $=\frac{3.92}{392} \times \frac{1}{100} \times 1000=0.1 \mathrm{~N}$
20 mL of 0.1 N salt solution $\equiv 18 \mathrm{~mL}$ of $\mathrm{KMnO}_4$ solution
20 mL of 0.1 N salt solution $\equiv 18 \mathrm{~mL}$ of $\mathrm{KMnO}_4$ solution
$\therefore$ Normality of $\mathrm{KMnO}_4$ solution $=\frac{20 \times 0.1}{18}\begin{array}{r}\therefore \text { Normality of } \mathrm{KMnO}_4 \text { solution }=\frac{20 \times 0.1}{18} \\ \quad=\frac{1}{9} \mathrm{~N}\end{array}
$\begin{aligned} \therefore \text { Strength of } \mathrm{KMnO}_4 \text { solution } & =\frac{1}{9} \times 31.6 \\ & =3.5 \mathrm{~g} \mathrm{~L}^{-1}\end{aligned}
